# Generated or fetched trees. Nothing here is written by hand, so reformatting
# it would only produce diffs that hide the changes that matter.
dist/
node_modules/
target/
third-party/
Cargo.lock
package-lock.json

# Written by `tauri-build` on every build: the permission schemas the capability
# files are validated against.
/apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen/

# Prose. The repository's Markdown is hand-wrapped to a column that keeps a
# `git diff` readable, and Prettier's own wrapping disagrees with it - running
# it over the documentation would rewrite every file for no gain and bury the
# real change in a reflow. Markdown is covered by .editorconfig instead.
*.md

# Everything outside the npm workspace. Prettier formats TypeScript, CSS, HTML
# and the JSON that configures them; Rust is rustfmt's and the workflows,
# scripts and issue templates are hand-written YAML that Prettier would
# re-indent for its own reasons.
/.github/
/crates/
/docs/
/scripts/
/tests/
/test-apps/

# Vendored verbatim from the Clipped design project so that a change made there
# can be diffed against this file. Reformatting it would break that comparison.
/packages/ui/src/styles/tokens.css
